Kent Paul Dolan wrote:
> "Quothz" <quothz@yahoo.com> wrote:

> So, I started taking detailed notes, one game out
> of every several.

Wow, that's a -lot- of detail. It's good stuff, though.
I took notes for the first five years or so, but not of
the same nature as yours - I wrote down oracularities,
item effects, fortunes, and suchlike, but never specific
details.

I suspect that taking brief notes is a useful tool for
both memory reconstruction and forced methodical play.
Taking longer notes could easily detract from the benefits
by distracting your focus and extending the game in real
time tremendously, totally aside from being a pain in the
ass.

But they were interesting to look through, and of course
posting 'em would be a good way to get critiques. I agree
with a lot of Klaus' points, and have to wonder whether you've
picked up poison resistance somewhere - I wouldn't be drinking
unidentified potions without it.

(It was particularly interesting to see how the character
was generated and what thoughts you had as a result.)

